    "lawCode": "Amd §722-b, County L",
    "lawSection": "County Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3527\n\nSPONSOR: BAILEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the county law, in relation to entitled compensation for\nclient representation\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe bill would allow the New York State Division of Criminal Justice\nServices to set, on an annual basis, the hourly rate of compensation for\nassigned counsel.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends Section 722-b of the County Law is to provide the\nDivision of Criminal Justice Services the authority to set the hourly\ncompensation rate for assigned counsel in the state. The Division of\nCriminal Justices Services shall review the hourly compensation rate on\nan annual basis and shall adjust the rate at:\n\n1) No less that 60 percent of the hourly rate of Federal Defenders for\nthe applicable fiscal year for misdemeanors or lessor offenses;\n\n2) No less than 90 percent of the hourly rate of Federal Defenders for\nthe applicable fiscal year for all other cases governed by the article.\n\nProvides that the Division of Criminal Justice Services has the authori-\nty to waive an increase in the assigned counsel compensation rates in\nany given year, but that assigned counsel compensation rates may not\nfall below the 60 and 90 percent thresholds for any given three-year\nperiod.\n\nProvides that counsel shall receive reimbursement for expenses reason-\nably incurred.\n\nSection 2: Provides that each claim for compensation and reimbursement\nshall be supported by a sworn statement and prohibits counsel from seek-\ning or accepting fees for representation without court approval.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe 18-b panels throughout NYS consist of attorneys who are certified by\nthe Appellate Division to handle all cases in Family Court, Surrogate\nCourt, Supreme Court, and Criminal Court, representing children and\nadults in multifaceted cases where families and liberties are at risk of\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
